[{:db/id "q-160866/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "cbee640b-a95d-5f36-8f8c-3373fc92993b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160866/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9ee5c590-1042-5faa-b633-57fa5b5a8af2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160866/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "00dcddd8-ebfd-5c34-98ec-c9c1418284a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160866/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c8308f24-2099-5ec8-80b2-960d497009c0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160866/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "048b116d-bb91-59ae-b961-45ef3fa4b588" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160866/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "12eab755-1d62-5455-bb52-18e7f27dab8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160866/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-160866/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-160866/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-160866/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-160866/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-160866/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160866" :question/id #uuid "15b63522-0c12-5bc3-a318-dae5fc4b32c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160866" :question/problem "Let $W$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=1.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $q(x)\\in W,$ where $q(x)={x}^{2}+1.$\n- For any $p(x)\\in W$ and $k\\in R,$ we have $k\\cdot p(x)\\in W.$\n- The set $W$ is closed under scalar multiplication." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q(x)={x}^{2}+1\\in W$ because\n\n$$\nq(0)=(0)^{2}+1=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. There exists a function in $W$ that has a scalar multiple not in $W.$ For example, let $p(x)={x}^{2}+1$ and $k=2.$ Notice that $p(x)$ belongs to $W$ since $p(0)=1.$ However, \n\n$$\n2\\cdot p(0)=2\\cdot ({0}^{2}+1)=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n Hence, $k\\cdot p(x)\\notin W.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160866/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160866"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94694"] :question/problem "Let $U$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $h(x)\\in U,$ where $h(x)=3x.$\n- For any $p(x)\\in U$ and $k\\in R,$ we have $k\\cdot p(x)\\in U.$\n- The set is closed under scalar multiplication." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $U$ contains only polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3},$ where $a$ is a real coefficient. However, $h(x)=3x$ is *not* a polynomial of this form. So, $h(x)\\notin U.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, suppose $p(x)=a{x}^{3}\\in U,$ where $a$ is a real coefficient, and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\nk\\cdot p(x)=k(a{x}^{3})=(ka){x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nSince $(ka)$ is a real coefficient, we conclude that $(ka){x}^{3}\\in U,$ i.e., $k\\cdot p(x)\\in U.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set is closed scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-160874/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "ee4c1126-8243-5658-a5d0-04c6cfc0b37d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160874/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "607740d3-0353-5136-8f0c-28b5716ab01f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160874/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "55cbf3ce-7176-5336-9424-0148e3859d29" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160874/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "5bbf210a-84b5-5965-adcb-010aa5be0c47" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160874/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "71d2cf6f-c9ac-5a1b-8b3e-af2428b42b6e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160874/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e624988-1c8d-5fdc-820b-91eef2d00a94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160874/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-160874/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-160874/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-160874/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-160874/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-160874/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160874" :question/id #uuid "cb166f23-b254-521c-b0cc-1d17dee65abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-160874" :question/problem "Let $C$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients whose degree is less than or equal to $2.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $g(x)\\in C,$ where $g(x)={x}^{3}$\n- For every $p(x),q(x)\\in C,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)\\in C.$\n- The set is closed under addition." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $C$ contains only polynomials whose degree is less than or equal to $2,$ however\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{deg}⁡({x}^{3})=3>2.\n$$\n\nSo, $g(x)={x}^{3}\\notin C.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, suppose $p(x),q(x)\\in C,$ then $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p(x))\\le 2$ and $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(q(x))\\le 2.$ Since $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p+q)$ is less than or equal to the maximum of the degrees of $p$ and $q$, we deduce that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p+q)\\le 2.\n$$\n\nHence, $p(x)+q(x)\\in C.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set is closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160874/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160874"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-160861/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "d3b8bf9b-3359-58a2-81f8-44ba8f1a56b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160861/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "acce2ad7-4ac7-5970-a743-89273d864945" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160861/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9a4509b7-1334-5a79-9a08-5ad5b05b2e67" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160861/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "7de40741-cf1e-5c83-89c4-65cbaa869262" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160861/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "8239421b-d8d3-5944-91c5-fe78a7c68f71" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-160861/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa95a4ac-6bfb-5e7d-9774-948048284a6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-160861/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-160861/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-160861/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-160861/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-160861/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-160861/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-160861" :question/id #uuid "6f7c3c39-8a1a-5a06-82f0-07fdf953c652" :question/math-academy-id "q-160861" :question/problem "Let $K$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=-1.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $p(x)\\in K,$ where $p(x)=(x-1)^{3}.$\n- For any $f(x),g(x)\\in K$, we have $f(x)+g(x)\\in K.$\n- The set is closed under addition." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $p(x)=(x-1)^{3}\\in K$ because \n\n$$\np(0)=(0-1)^{3}=(-1)^{3}=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. There exist functions in $K$ such that their sum is *not* in $K.$ For example, let $f(x)=-1$ and $g(x)=(x-1)^{3}.$ Notice that both these functions belong to $K$ since $f(0)=g(0)=-1.$ However,\n\n$$\nf(0)+g(0)=-1+(0-1)^{3}=-2\\ne -1.\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x)+g(x)\\notin K.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is *not* closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-160861/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-160861"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-43859/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "96f28374-50d2-5eb3-bddf-8e6eb514a5e6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43859/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "3b7e8965-d181-5f32-8451-0deac8c0cff6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43859/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" :answer/id #uuid "56ac0766-2fb8-5197-94b9-fa2143aeadc2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43859/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "01176b20-1014-5569-9e31-47827a7755e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43859/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "91de564a-48cc-536d-8949-26f7ed45d9a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43859/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9544c342-fa35-56f7-bcf9-490b56d4bcca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-43859/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-43859/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-43859/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-43859/selection/03b99debc8e9534f2364927a2cf1eba83bddd906503dea5d13395ce906a45ab9" "q-43859/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-43859/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-43859" :question/id #uuid "79a70322-eda4-52ca-9b62-4aa2732797d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-43859" :question/problem "Let $W$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $q(x)\\in W,$ where $q(x)={2}^{x}.$\n- For any $f(x)\\in W$ and $k\\in R,$ we have $k\\cdot f(x)\\in W.$\n- The set is closed under scalar multiplication." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q(x)={2}^{x}\\in W$ because\n\n$$\nq(0)={2}^{0}=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. There exists a function in $W$ that has a scalar multiple *not* in $W.$ For example, let $f(x)={2}^{x}$ and $k=2.$ Notice that $f(x)$ belongs to $W$ since $f(0)=1.$ However,\n\n$$\n2\\cdot f(0)=2\\cdot {2}^{0}=2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nHence, $k\\cdot f(x)\\notin W.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-43859/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43859"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162392/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "277a455c-bae0-5bf0-9c74-9bbcea84ec1d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162392/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "8c07f0b8-7dc4-51e7-a8f7-468f278e94cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162392/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "a40af82b-1a0e-5796-b298-cc157c1ac546" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162392/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "eecf481c-a5aa-52da-827e-d1ef87f61244" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162392/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "7e87ef15-5040-5357-9d42-f273a518fc58" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162392/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "768e8cfa-0672-5d76-8ea9-35968dde51ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162392/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-162392/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-162392/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-162392/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-162392/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-162392/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162392" :question/id #uuid "792ebea3-f1c3-5e2d-879b-40efc7334917" :question/math-academy-id "q-162392" :question/problem "Let $U$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3}+b{x}^{2},$ where $a,b\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The zero-polynomial belongs to $U.$\n- For any $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have $p(x)-q(x)=q(x)-p(x).$\n- There are polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in U$ such that $[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)\\ne p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the zero-polynomial can be represented as \n\n$$\n0=0\\cdot {x}^{3}+0\\cdot {x}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \nHence, $0\\in U.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the polynomials $p(x)={x}^{3}\\in U$ and the zero-polynomial $q(x)=0\\in U.$ Then \n\n$$\np(x)-q(x)=p(x)-0={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nwhile \n\n$$\nq(x)-p(x)=0-p(x)=-{x}^{3}\\ne {x}^{3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have \n\n$$\n[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)=p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)],\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162392/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162392"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-74700"] :question/problem "Let $U$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{3},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The zero-polynomial belongs to $U.$\n- For any $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x).$\n- For any $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in U,$ we have $[p(x)-q(x)]-r(x)=p(x)-[q(x)-r(x)].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the zero-polynomial can be represented as \n\n$$\n0=0\\cdot {x}^{3}.\n$$\n\n \nHence, $0\\in U.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in U,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)=q(x)+p(x)\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is commutative.\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, consider polynomials $p(x)={x}^{3},$ $q(x)=2{x}^{3},$ and $r(x)=3{x}^{3}$ from $U.$ Then: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[p(x)-q(x)]-r(x) & =[{x}^{3}-2{x}^{3}]-3{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-3{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-4{x}^{3} \\\\ p(x)-[q(x)-r(x)] & ={x}^{3}-[2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{3}] \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-[-{x}^{3}] \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $[p(x)-q(x)]-r(x)\\ne p(x)-[q(x)-r(x)].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94686/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "81ad2104-e727-51e3-9cb0-dfa4b35719ca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94686/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e9837c11-4383-5086-8c41-4081dcf85e14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94686/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "31824c0a-e99c-50cf-a290-90f47ade59c3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94686/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "db2368b9-c86a-57a1-8910-b58ea2038110" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94686/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "10e660ce-90f3-5b17-8a59-411ccc7a67ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94686/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "140afd88-1bae-57de-945c-fd3daa91d0e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94686/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-94686/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-94686/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-94686/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-94686/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-94686/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94686" :question/id #uuid "035f42c4-f483-51a4-ad6b-f46547f41ecf" :question/math-academy-id "q-94686" :question/problem "Let $E$ be the set of polynomials of the form $a{x}^{2}+1,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The constant polynomial $1$ belongs to $E.$\n- For the constant polynomial $1$ and any $p(x)\\in E,$ we have $1+p(x)=p(x).$\n- There are polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x)\\in E$ such that $[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)\\ne p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the constant polynomial $1$ can be represented as\n\n$$\n1=0\\cdot {x}^{2}+1.\n$$\n\nHence, $1\\in E.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}+1\\in E.$ Then, \n\n$$\n1+p(x)=1+{x}^{2}+1={x}^{2}+2\\ne p(x).\n$$\n\nThe zero-polynomial $0$ is the unique polynomial such that for any $p(x)\\in E$ we have $0+p(x)=p(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false. For any polynomials $p(x),q(x)\\in E,$ we have \n\n$$\n[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x)=p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)],\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94686/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94686"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94649/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "655dccb1-b3b3-5aa5-8f2f-06abb4c197af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94649/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "7df87f18-3990-52c0-bce9-cd0ffa554069" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94649/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "5c095616-2c46-5774-b4d5-60c2697ff444" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94649/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "2da73cfc-c4fd-5400-bf14-ebf78d6216bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94649/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ee59f476-3097-5a82-8125-a260dcbb7304" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94649/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a68bd26e-3789-535f-861e-cdf4cefee6b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94649/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-94649/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-94649/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-94649/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-94649/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-94649/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94649" :question/id #uuid "4de4ed8a-e25a-599c-88bb-6ed0a739caa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-94649" :question/problem "Let $N$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=0.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The constant function $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in R$ belongs to $N.$\n- For any $f(t),g(t)\\in N,$ we have $f(t)-g(t)=g(t)-f(t).$\n- The addition of functions in $N$ is commutative." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $N$ contains only functions that evaluate to zero at zero. However, the function defined by $f(x)=1$ for all $x\\in R$ satisfies $f(0)=1\\ne 0.$ So, $f\\notin N.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider functions $f(t)=2t$ and $g(t)=t$ in $N.$ Then:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)-g(t) & =2t-t \\\\  & =t \\\\ g(t)-f(t) & =t-2t \\\\  & =-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(t)-g(t)\\ne g(t)-f(t).$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(t),g(t)\\in N,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(t)+g(t)=g(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nsince the addition of functions is commutative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94649/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94649"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106703/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "4c99e194-8549-5641-b44c-d047f68946f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106703/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "6a0e2ace-c045-5dde-9033-6dca7f98410a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106703/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "872cc488-3cd3-5fd3-b41a-e12bb9d3aa9e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106703/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "682da299-b46b-57aa-a00f-9f95425f307e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106703/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "4d206173-bc07-5302-b5ca-36686727c107" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106703/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ac9c1a2-b86a-51c0-8bf5-5d12f8459fa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106703/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-106703/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-106703/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-106703/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-106703/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-106703/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106703" :question/id #uuid "4ba64f9d-284e-5897-88b7-47c3b80dee0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-106703" :question/problem "Let $T$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients and whose degree is at most $10.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- For the zero-polynomial $0$ and any $p(x)\\in T,$ we have $p(x)+0=0.$\n- For any $p(x),q(x)\\in T$, we have $p(x)+q(x)=p(x)-q(x).$\n- For any polynomial $p(x)\\in T$ we have $-p(x)\\in T$ such that $p(x)+(-p(x))=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}$ in $T.$ Then,\n\n$$\np(x)+0={x}^{2}+0={x}^{2}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, consider the polynomials $p(x)=q(x)={x}^{2}\\in T.$\nThen:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x)+q(x) & ={x}^{2}+{x}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2} \\\\ p(x)-q(x) & ={x}^{2}-{x}^{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $p(x)+q(x)\\ne p(x)-q(x).$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any polynomial $p(x)\\in T,$ there is a corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ such that\n\n$$\np(x)+(-p(x))=p(x)-p(x)=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{deg}⁡(-p(x))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p(x))\\le 10,\n$$\n\nhence $-p(x)\\in T.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106703/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb09138-45df-5e6c-87af-772980ff7546"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106703"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162664/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "035c3833-093a-5727-9117-6a446206baed" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162664/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "086057e1-a93e-5bdd-881e-75af57578eaf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162664/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "55f81e13-921d-5c88-8d48-ca8a590450c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162664/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "d4bf6260-2ec7-5521-a8b4-f0e18979be64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162664/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "500fbe06-4c26-5e2f-84e8-64ae54266437" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162664/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "32f6fbed-8405-5d7d-b12e-769fa19e441f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162664/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-162664/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-162664/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-162664/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-162664/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-162664/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162664" :question/id #uuid "d2a4d327-a5a5-5020-b145-bcfacb320a74" :question/math-academy-id "q-162664" :question/problem "Let $Q$ be the set of all functions of the form $f(x)=a{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There is a function $f(x)\\in Q,$ such that $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n- For any $f(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$\n- For any $f(x),g(x)\\in Q$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Consider the null function $f(x)=0=0{x}^{2}\\in Q.$ Then,\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot f(x)=(-1)\\cdot 0=0=f(x).\n$$\n\nHence, $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any function $f(x)\\in Q$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(x),g(x)\\in Q$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the results of $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162664/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162664"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-106809/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "0e61b3ed-957d-5a3e-9e91-48d2bb6f4f84" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106809/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "55dbca2f-c827-57e4-a4c7-530e15d21e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106809/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "5b4f32b2-356a-5f6e-9257-9bcd0e14ed34" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106809/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "08bbaaf1-0052-57c8-b3b8-f1f9468970ef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106809/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "34e180de-32d2-50bd-a482-84a8899e360e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106809/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "168ac4ae-bb2e-5d82-92fa-a879f128930a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106809/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-106809/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-106809/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-106809/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-106809/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-106809/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106809" :question/id #uuid "04d5ce9f-b494-5a36-b055-91916446f85d" :question/math-academy-id "q-106809" :question/problem "Let $N$ be the set of all functions of the form $f(x)=a|x|,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- For any $f(x)\\in N,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n- For any $f(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$\n- For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, consider $f(x)=|x|\\in N.$ Then,\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot f(x)=(-1)\\cdot |x|=-|x|\\ne |x|.\n$$\n\nHence, $(-1)\\cdot f(x)\\ne f(x).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any function $f(x)\\in N$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(x),g(x)\\in N$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the results of $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106809/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106809"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162668/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "5d037d73-4758-553f-b999-5a87c7fff68f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162668/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ccb0fa37-4676-5b5f-bceb-ec7cbad08f3b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162668/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "bcd63c6e-1036-59b0-8f0d-15114487c0bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162668/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "6fac000c-3a74-5415-9509-438149e4e660" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162668/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "c18ab1b7-1baf-59b6-90de-99757e36f680" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162668/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d58db4d-3721-5c70-aac0-6ff33d452d46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162668/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-162668/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-162668/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-162668/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-162668/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-162668/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162668" :question/id #uuid "dbb1f4fc-787a-54da-88f6-e220b9e104e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-162668" :question/problem "Let $Y$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ real matrices with determinant $1.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- For any $A\\in Y,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot A=-A.$\n- For any $A\\in Y$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$\n- For any $A\\in Y$ we have $2A\\in Y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in Y,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, we have\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot {a}_{ij}=-{a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot A=-A.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in Y,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta ){a}_{ij}=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+\\beta {a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, the identity matrix ${I}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\in Y,$ however $2{I}_{2}\\notin Y$ because\n\n$$\n|2{I}_{2}|=|2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 0=4\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162668/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162668"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-106806"] :question/problem "Let $S$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ real matrices with determinant $1.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\n- For any $A\\in S,$ we have $1\\cdot A=A.$\n- For any $A\\in S$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.$\n- There is a matrix $A\\in S$ such that $\\frac{1}{2}(2A)\\ne A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in S,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, we have\n\n$$\n1\\cdot {a}_{ij}={a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot A=A.\n$$\n\n- Statements II is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A=({a}_{ij})\\in S,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta ){a}_{ij}=\\alpha {a}_{ij}+\\beta {a}_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )A=\\alpha A+\\beta A.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. For a matrix in $A\\in S,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(2A)=(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2)A=1\\cdot A=A\n$$\n\nsince the scalar multiplication of matrices is associative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-106812/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "34ffdbc3-9526-53d0-8808-92480b04c81a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106812/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "78a323ec-1bff-52e0-aa26-a7c41449453c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106812/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "25f50716-9439-5d5a-9f81-86038f5e1973" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106812/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "046f8140-7203-59dc-8829-5d4066704ad9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106812/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "be171e2a-aeb9-579e-b3f2-dc732c8dc382" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-106812/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "be03e7c9-e9ab-5d13-b77b-c0962c66a8ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-106812/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-106812/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-106812/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-106812/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-106812/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-106812/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-106812" :question/id #uuid "db7c1fae-b77a-5238-b170-21030fe2e82d" :question/math-academy-id "q-106812" :question/problem "Let $G$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)>0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- For any $f(x)\\in G,$ we have $1\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$\n- For any $f(x)\\in G$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$, we have $(\\alpha -\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)-\\beta f(x).$\n- The scalar multiplication of functions in $G$ is associative." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in G$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus,\n\n$$\n(1\\cdot f)(x)=1\\cdot f(x)=f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in G$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha -\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)-\\beta f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in G$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta f(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )f(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-106812/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-106812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9960"] :question/problem "Let $M$ be the set of all $2\\times2$ real matrices whose entries are non-negative. Then, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $I_2 \\in M$\n\n- For any $A \\in M$ and $\\alpha \\in \\mathbb{R}$, we have $\\alpha \\cdot A \\in M.$\n\n- The set is closed under scalar multiplication." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/assets/191451016703b3287c7e58fdb59e22effb919c97dcad7a9e3bec09efd115795a.png) because all its entries are non-negative.\n\n- Statement II is false. There exists a $2\\times2$ real matrix in $M$ that has a scalar multiple not in $M.$ \n\nFor example, let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/assets/3b13b13c14eb335adb58b3d1ff3132b4e189065033481aaf371a9376188f2443.png) and $\\alpha=-1\\in\\mathbb{R}.$ Notice that $A$ belongs to $M$ since statement I is true. However,\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044323/assets/a906a8520f0b2f676bcf97411232fa3303f87aec9dcae9abe19dca00ab6da1a7.png)\nSince the entries on the main diagonal are negative, we conclude that $-1 \\cdot A \\notin M.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4787"] :question/problem "Let $L$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients whose degree is less than or equal to $2.$  Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- For any $p(x),q(x) \\in L,$ we have $p(x)+q(x) = q(x)+p(x).$\n\n- For any $p(x),q(x),r(x) \\in L,$ we have $[p(x)+q(x)]+r(x) = p(x)+[q(x)+r(x)].$\n\n- For each $p(x) \\in L,$ we have $-p(x) \\in L$ such that $p(x)+(-p(x))=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any polynomials $p(x), q(x) \\in L,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\np(x) + q(x)= q(x) +p(x)\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is commutative.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any polynomials $p(x),q(x),r(x) \\in L,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n[p(x) + q(x)] + r(x) = p(x) + [q(x) + r(x)]\n$$\n\nsince polynomial addition is associative.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any polynomial $p(x) \\in L,$ there is a corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ such that\n\n$$\np(x) + (-p(x))= p(x) - p(x) = 0.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\deg(-p(x)) = \\deg(p(x)) \\leq 2,\n$$\n\nhence $-p(x) \\in L.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8229"] :question/problem "Let $P$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ real matrices $A= (a_{ij})$ such that $a_{11} + a_{22} > 0.$ Which of the following properties are true?\n\n- For any $A \\in P,$ we have $1 \\cdot A = A.$\n\n- For any $A \\in P$ and $\\alpha,\\beta \\in \\mathbb{R},$ we have $\\alpha(\\beta A) = (\\alpha\\beta) A.$\n\n- For any $A \\in P$ and $\\alpha,\\beta \\in \\mathbb{R},$ we have $(\\alpha+\\beta) A= \\alpha A + \\beta A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A = (a_{ij}) \\in P,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, we have\n\n$$\n1 \\cdot a_{ij} = a_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot A=A.\n$$\n\n- Statements II is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A = (a_{ij}) \\in P,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha, \\beta \\in \\mathbb{R},$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha(\\beta a_{ij}) = (\\alpha\\beta) a_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n\\alpha(\\beta A) = (\\alpha\\beta) A.\n$$\n\n- Statements III is true. Indeed, for any $2\\times 2$ matrix $A = (a_{ij}) \\in P,$ the entries are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha, \\beta \\in \\mathbb{R},$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha+\\beta) a_{ij} = \\alpha a_{ij} + \\beta a_{ij},\n$$\n\nand hence,\n\n$$\n(\\alpha+\\beta) A= \\alpha A + \\beta A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
